<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lambert of Italy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 880–898</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Lambert of Spoleto</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lambert (c. 880–898), of the Widonid dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spoleto">Spoleto</a>, became King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 891 and was crowned emperor by Pope Formosus in 892 as co-ruler with his father, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guy-iii-of-spoleto">Guy of Spoleto</a>. After Guy's death in 894 he ruled alone, contesting Italy with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berengar-i-of-italy">Berengar of Friuli</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnulf-of-carinthia">Arnulf of Carinthia</a>, until he died in a hunting accident in 898.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lambert-of-italy.jpg" alt="Lambert of Italy" width="290" height="305" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johannes Berardi (chronicon casauriense) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Four_kings_of_Italy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
